														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3965285">
									

<p>I still remember that morning like it was yesterday. Was in the middle of an English test when the news came in via a hushed whisper to our teacher. And even though I knew <strong>something</strong> was off the teacher wouldn't tell me what until everyone finished the test. Longest few minutes of my life.</p>
<p>We turned on the TV afterwards and were in conversation about if it was an accident or not when the 2nd plane hit the south tower and I remember that moment with perfect clarity even after all those years. We went from loud speculation and murmuring to dead silence for a good twenty seconds.</p>
<p>Even at the age of 14 and 15 we all knew that the whole world had changed. We just didn't know how yet.</p>
<p>+1</p>

