			<div class="content" id="post-content-3965372">
									

<p>This doesn't come across as jingoism, but I'm sceptical that it's possible to write a story about 9/11 without conveying something about the wider political context, even unintentionally - or, perhaps that the idea that depoliticising 9/11 is <em>possible</em> is itself a political position (and one I disagree with).</p>
<p>In any case, there are certainly an endless stream of 9/11 narratives ostensibly about individual sacrifice that are trying to advance various political ends. I don't think this article makes those implications, but maybe these have poisoned the well for me.</p>

